 A general approach for applying sequential data compression schemes to blocks of data, decoded on-the-fly by the GPU in a single render pass by decomposing blocks into parallel stripes.
 
+### GPU Pre-Decompression (Full Block)
+A method where all compressed data blocks required for the current rendering frame are transferred to the GPU and fully decompressed using CUDA programming before rendering begins [S4, unofficial]. The pipeline consists of three steps: 1. Transfer: Import compressed tensor blocks to the GPU. 2. Decompress: Use CUDA programming to decompress the data. 3. Render: Use the decompressed data for visualization [S4, unofficial]. It was used by Suter et al. and Wetekam et al. (using FPGA hardware) [S4, unofficial].
+
 ## Operating characteristics
 *   **Time Complexity:** Real-time performance is achieved on standard graphics PCs for massive datasets (e.g., 256GB turbulence simulation compressed to <2GB) [S1, S3, unofficial]. The complexity is dominated by the adaptive loading, decoding, and filtering per frame [S1, S3, unofficial].
